{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Supersedes bug e983 (config_manual fire-and-forget) by generalizing it into an infra-health readiness gate for the review/landing pipeline.\n\nPRINCIPLE: an unhealthy infra precondition (unapplied/invalid config, LLM-provider outage, GitHub outage, env error) makes LLM Review UNSOUND. Treat these as INFRA-CLASS conditions (per Zuul RETRY_LIMIT/NODE_FAILURE): block fail-closed, do NOT cast a content vote, and AUTO-RECOVER (re-run blocked reviews) when the signal returns healthy — no human recheck (author changed nothing; only the environment did).\n\nDESIGN (OSS-grounded):\n- Health registry: named checks, each tri-state healthy/unhealthy/unknown (never conflate 'check errored' with 'healthy'). Signals: config-applied (live-vs-desired refs-meta/replication probe), config-valid, llm-provider (Anthropic reachable/quota), github (API/Actions/mirror), deploy-host/replication, environment.\n- Aggregator: per-signal blocking vs advisory severity; fail-closed on any blocking-unhealthy. (cf. Argo health assessment; K8s readiness gate.)\n- Consumption points, one health source: (a) REVIEW boundary — review-bot ABSTAINS (casts no LLM-Review content vote) when infra unhealthy, instead of erroring/false-voting; (b) LANDING boundary — dedicated bot-cast Infra-Ready submit-requirement blocks submit with an explicit per-signal message. Keeps env-readiness OFF the code-content labels (avoids the 'environment masquerading as a review vote' anti-pattern).\n- Recovery = infra-class retry loop: on signal recovery, auto-re-run blocked reviews + re-eval gate; bounded (RETRY_LIMIT), windowed (thundering-herd), same-patchset re-vote that cleanly REPLACES the stale -1, terminal alert on exhaustion. (cf. Zuul infra-class auto-retry.)\n- Reliability: independent tri-state observation (Ansible/Puppet lesson: apply exit-0 != converged; only a zero-diff re-read proves it); Terraform-style tri-state so a probe ERROR never false-clears; marker bound to the config revision it was computed against (Terraform stale-plan rejection).\n- Waiver + break-glass: audited per-signal/global override; guard-the-guard on who may waive (Gatekeeper); a guaranteed break-glass reachable when the gate itself is wedged.\n- Rollout: WARN/detect-only first (emit signals, do not block) until detection proven reliable, THEN flip to fail-closed. Staged config-first.\n\nCONTEXT: closes the e983 root cause properly (durable reconciled status, not a fire-and-forget event) and also turns today's ad-hoc LLM/GitHub-outage failures into one loud, self-healing, auditable signal. Related: 0e15 (--class propagation), and the plan-review calibration miss on epic 86ac/ed13 that let consumer-migration advisories ship sub-threshold.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A health registry exposes each named infra check in tri-state (healthy / unhealthy / unknown) and never reports a probe error as healthy; verified by a unit test that feeds an errored probe and asserts the aggregate is unknown, not healthy.\n- [ ] When any blocking signal is unhealthy the review-bot casts no LLM-Review content vote (abstains) and the Infra-Ready submit-requirement blocks submit with a per-signal message; verified by an offline test asserting no content vote is emitted and submit is blocked.\n- [ ] On signal recovery a blocked review is automatically re-run under a bounded retry (RETRY_LIMIT) with windowed replay, replacing the stale vote without human recheck; verified by a test that drives unhealthy then healthy and asserts exactly one bounded re-run.\n- [ ] Each health observation is bound to the config revision it was computed against and a stale observation is rejected rather than allowed to false-clear; verified by a test that presents a stale-revision observation and asserts rejection.\n- [ ] Rollout ships in WARN/detect-only mode (signals emitted, submit not blocked) until a config flip enables fail-closed; verified by a test asserting detect-only emits signals without blocking and the flip enables blocking.\n- [ ] An audited break-glass override can waive per-signal or global blocking and remains reachable when the gate itself is wedged; verified by a test exercising the waiver path and asserting the audit record is written."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786070188815562001,"uuid":"d355cb16-142f-46d4-9c46-7f1fa5b23e16"}